1
00:01:58,625 --> 00:02:03,000
DELUSION

2
00:02:12,666 --> 00:02:14,625
So how has this caught fire?

3
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:20,041
Um, not sure. It's not
the right time for forest fires.

4
00:02:21,208 --> 00:02:22,666
Not this time of the year.

5
00:02:23,208 --> 00:02:25,125
It's much more likely that it was arson.

6
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:27,916
You see here? The ground's damp.

7
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:29,916
Hmm.

8
00:02:38,208 --> 00:02:40,541
Inspector, something here.

9
00:02:41,291 --> 00:02:42,291
Come on through.

10
00:02:59,958 --> 00:03:02,500
<i>The victim's teeth were also taken out.</i>

11
00:03:02,583 --> 00:03:05,666
<i>Cases like this</i>
<i>have happened in other provinces.</i>

12
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:09,083
<i>And in every case,</i>
<i>teeth were missing from the bodies.</i>

13
00:03:09,708 --> 00:03:10,875
<i>Forensics.</i>

14
00:03:10,958 --> 00:03:14,250
<i>We found skeletal remains</i>
<i>near this large tree wrapped in cloth.</i>

15
00:03:14,333 --> 00:03:15,833
<i>- Copy, over.</i>
- Copy that.

16
00:03:39,958 --> 00:03:41,791
- What's up, Wan?
- Wat.

17
00:03:46,041 --> 00:03:47,208
I've got Dad with me.

18
00:03:48,166 --> 00:03:50,000
Can I take him to stay at your place?

19
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:53,708
Uh-- What? Hang on. What happened?

20
00:03:55,041 --> 00:03:57,250
We can't leave Dad with Mom anymore.

21
00:03:57,333 --> 00:04:00,666
<i>Sis, calm down. Tell me what happened.</i>

22
00:04:02,416 --> 00:04:04,250
I think Mom killed Uncle Sak.

23
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:17,250
Doctor, the next patient's here.
Shall I send her in?

24
00:04:18,666 --> 00:04:20,541
Just give me a second, okay?

25
00:04:20,625 --> 00:04:21,625
Sure.

26
00:04:23,541 --> 00:04:24,791
Okay. Just stay calm.

27
00:04:24,875 --> 00:04:27,625
<i>Don't take Dad too far away yet.</i>

28
00:04:27,708 --> 00:04:31,208
<i>An unfamiliar environment</i>
<i>might make him delirious.</i>

29
00:04:31,291 --> 00:04:34,875
Just find a place you can stay nearby.

30
00:04:34,958 --> 00:04:37,916
I'll be there as soon as I can, okay, sis?

31
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,208
Just take it easy there.

32
00:04:39,791 --> 00:04:41,375
Okay. I'll go to the lake house.

33
00:04:42,583 --> 00:04:43,583
Come soon, Wat.

34
00:05:12,041 --> 00:05:13,041
You again.

35
00:05:15,666 --> 00:05:17,916
A fire broke out on your property.
Did you know that?

36
00:05:20,333 --> 00:05:21,291
Did it?

37
00:05:22,166 --> 00:05:23,875
If I'd known, I would have put it out.

38
00:05:26,250 --> 00:05:27,583
Listen to me.

39
00:05:27,666 --> 00:05:30,333
Human remains
have been found on your land.

40
00:05:30,416 --> 00:05:33,000
You can't just keep saying
you don't know anything.

41
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:34,250
Remains?

42
00:05:38,041 --> 00:05:38,875
Okay.

43
00:05:39,916 --> 00:05:43,041
The hut that burned down
and the human remains

44
00:05:43,125 --> 00:05:45,250
were both found on your land.

45
00:05:45,333 --> 00:05:47,500
As of now,
your entire family are suspects.

46
00:05:47,583 --> 00:05:49,125
You all need to come the station.

47
00:05:49,208 --> 00:05:51,125
Where have your husband and kids gone?

48
00:05:54,833 --> 00:05:55,750
I don't know.

49
00:05:56,708 --> 00:05:58,041
They've left me here alone.

50
00:06:05,833 --> 00:06:06,833
Come on, Nee.

51
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,500
INSPECTOR SASIDIT

52
00:06:48,583 --> 00:06:49,583
CALL ENDED

53
00:08:42,833 --> 00:08:44,791
There was a corpse in your backyard.

54
00:08:44,875 --> 00:08:46,791
You're saying you have no idea.

55
00:08:51,083 --> 00:08:52,083
It's big.

56
00:08:53,750 --> 00:08:55,250
Someone could have got lost

57
00:08:56,041 --> 00:08:57,708
or dumped a body there.

58
00:08:58,583 --> 00:08:59,583
How would I know?

59
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:04,750
No one goes in there these days.

60
00:09:04,833 --> 00:09:07,208
What about this tin full of teeth?

61
00:09:07,291 --> 00:09:09,333
Can you explain how that got there?

62
00:09:13,791 --> 00:09:15,875
These are all the cases
from the last 20 years

63
00:09:15,958 --> 00:09:17,041
that I think are connected.

64
00:09:18,166 --> 00:09:19,541
In the first ten years,

65
00:09:20,458 --> 00:09:23,125
the victims were all found
within the same province.

66
00:09:23,208 --> 00:09:25,041
MYSTERIOUS SKELETON DISCOVERED

67
00:09:25,125 --> 00:09:26,625
And the ten years after that,

68
00:09:27,291 --> 00:09:31,083
bodies with missing teeth were found
across multiple provinces.

69
00:09:31,166 --> 00:09:32,625
POLICE TO SOLVE
MISSING PERSONS CASES

70
00:09:32,708 --> 00:09:34,958
All before Mued and Sak.

71
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:38,875
And our main suspect?
There is no record of him moving.

72
00:09:40,041 --> 00:09:41,291
Are you sure they're connected?

73
00:09:42,375 --> 00:09:44,125
I'm sure the person we're looking for

74
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:45,833
committed all of these murders.

75
00:09:49,375 --> 00:09:52,541
Well, if you need a warrant,
then just let me know.

76
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:54,500
Get this wrapped up.

77
00:09:55,416 --> 00:09:58,500
The news is already spreading.

78
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:36,541
That's Mom's car. Is she meeting us here?

79
00:10:40,083 --> 00:10:43,250
Aim! Just stay here.

80
00:10:45,208 --> 00:10:46,666
I'll go talk to your mom first.

81
00:10:48,166 --> 00:10:50,041
I'll bring her out to see you.

82
00:10:50,125 --> 00:10:51,375
I miss Mom.

83
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:53,541
Aim, don't. Stop!

84
00:10:56,708 --> 00:10:58,833
Stay here until I get back, understand?

85
00:11:02,541 --> 00:11:03,791
If you disobey…

86
00:11:05,916 --> 00:11:07,333
you won't see your mom again.

87
00:11:59,958 --> 00:12:00,833
What's that?

88
00:12:02,375 --> 00:12:03,708
What's that?

89
00:12:26,125 --> 00:12:27,416
Ah.

90
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:28,833
- You piece of shit.
- Ah!

91
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:31,958
You think?

92
00:12:34,375 --> 00:12:37,958
Your family's money was made
with my family name too, you know?

93
00:12:39,708 --> 00:12:41,208
Without my father's help,

94
00:12:42,250 --> 00:12:44,166
would you have even
got those plots of land

95
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:46,500
to squeeze your money out of?

96
00:12:55,708 --> 00:12:58,083
That family name you have…

97
00:13:00,333 --> 00:13:01,541
it's hardly worth a thing.

98
00:13:06,041 --> 00:13:07,541
And all…

99
00:13:07,625 --> 00:13:10,916
you ever wanted from me
is my family's money.

100
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,208
You piece of fucking trash!

101
00:13:14,291 --> 00:13:15,541
Fucking leech!

102
00:13:30,125 --> 00:13:32,000
You fucked her right here, yeah?

103
00:13:33,166 --> 00:13:34,333
You make me sick.

104
00:13:35,208 --> 00:13:36,708
So what, huh?

105
00:13:44,250 --> 00:13:45,541
You're gonna expose me?

106
00:13:48,166 --> 00:13:49,416
You wanna ruin me, huh?

107
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:54,083
Don't you love your son?

108
00:13:55,541 --> 00:13:58,458
Don't you love Aim?
Do you want to humiliate him?

109
00:14:01,541 --> 00:14:03,458
Do you really think I'm that fucked up?

110
00:14:04,125 --> 00:14:05,916
I would never do that.

111
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,500
But you're right about one thing.

112
00:14:08,458 --> 00:14:11,375
It's always been about the money.

113
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,583
But it didn't come for free.

114
00:14:16,166 --> 00:14:17,541
I traded my life…

115
00:14:18,916 --> 00:14:20,875
I traded all my dignity, so…

116
00:14:22,458 --> 00:14:23,833
I'm taking what I earned.

117
00:14:27,333 --> 00:14:28,333
Have your divorce…

118
00:14:29,708 --> 00:14:31,208
but Aim comes with me.

119
00:14:33,541 --> 00:14:34,541
Your family

120
00:14:35,458 --> 00:14:37,458
can't raise a decent human.

121
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:39,500
Just look at you.

122
00:14:41,833 --> 00:14:43,375
That's…

123
00:14:43,458 --> 00:14:44,500
Enough!

124
00:14:53,541 --> 00:14:55,250
You fucking leech!

125
00:15:45,541 --> 00:15:47,833
Please, Dad! No! No.

126
00:16:58,583 --> 00:16:59,583
Aim!

127
00:17:02,375 --> 00:17:03,750
Aunt Pannee.

128
00:17:03,833 --> 00:17:07,416
If you don't come clean,
you'll be tried as an accomplice

129
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:08,791
and go to jail.

130
00:17:23,166 --> 00:17:24,375
WANRUDEE

131
00:17:25,666 --> 00:17:26,500
Hello?

132
00:17:26,583 --> 00:17:28,791
<i>Please. Please help.</i>

133
00:17:28,875 --> 00:17:30,750
<i>Dad took my son away again.</i>

134
00:17:30,833 --> 00:17:32,583
Okay, stay calm. Where are you now?

135
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:34,333
Aim.

136
00:17:36,291 --> 00:17:37,291
Aim.

137
00:17:47,250 --> 00:17:48,250
Aim.

138
00:17:54,083 --> 00:17:55,083
Aim.

139
00:17:57,416 --> 00:17:58,250
Aim.

140
00:18:06,708 --> 00:18:07,708
Aim.

141
00:18:28,083 --> 00:18:28,916
Pa?

142
00:18:31,166 --> 00:18:32,041
Come out.

143
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:34,750
I won't hurt you, okay?

144
00:18:42,833 --> 00:18:43,833
Pa.

145
00:19:36,125 --> 00:19:37,333
Spread out and start looking.

146
00:19:37,958 --> 00:19:39,500
They can't have gone very far.

147
00:20:39,250 --> 00:20:40,791
Hey, sit down. Sit!

148
00:20:40,875 --> 00:20:42,458
LOEI FORWARD GROUP

149
00:20:42,541 --> 00:20:43,583
Go back and sit.

150
00:20:45,916 --> 00:20:46,833
He hasn't woken up

151
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,291
I said sit down.

152
00:21:15,791 --> 00:21:17,458
Mom didn't kill Sak, sis.

153
00:21:19,166 --> 00:21:20,166
She almost did.

154
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
She didn't finish.

155
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:33,916
Nee.

156
00:21:34,666 --> 00:21:35,583
Help…

157
00:21:36,416 --> 00:21:37,541
Help me.

158
00:22:09,625 --> 00:22:12,333
What are you, Phii Pong?
Eating a dead rat?

159
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:16,666
I'm not Pong. I wasn't.

160
00:22:16,750 --> 00:22:18,583
Then why are you poking it with a stick?

161
00:22:18,666 --> 00:22:20,291
Phii Pong has possessed you.

162
00:22:20,375 --> 00:22:22,166
I'm not Phii Pong. I wasn't eating it.

163
00:22:22,250 --> 00:22:23,583
Eat it!

164
00:22:23,666 --> 00:22:24,500
Get off!

165
00:22:26,166 --> 00:22:28,166
Eat it, Phii Pong!

166
00:22:29,625 --> 00:22:30,791
Eat it!

167
00:22:36,333 --> 00:22:37,291
Eat it!

168
00:23:06,166 --> 00:23:07,000
Hey!

169
00:23:10,083 --> 00:23:11,208
What?

170
00:23:13,833 --> 00:23:14,916
Don't!

171
00:23:21,125 --> 00:23:21,958
No!

172
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:31,958
Let me out!

173
00:23:33,416 --> 00:23:36,041
Let me out! I'm not Pong!

174
00:23:36,125 --> 00:23:37,125
Let me out!

175
00:24:04,750 --> 00:24:05,708
Hey!

176
00:24:07,041 --> 00:24:07,875
Hey!

177
00:25:39,041 --> 00:25:41,333
You remind me of Dad
when you make that face.

178
00:25:44,625 --> 00:25:45,458
Why?

179
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,083
Do I disgust you?

180
00:25:58,625 --> 00:25:59,583
I do get it.

181
00:26:02,041 --> 00:26:03,833
I never wanted to be like this.

182
00:26:05,458 --> 00:26:06,791
<i>But once I started,</i>

183
00:26:07,708 --> 00:26:09,541
<i>I couldn't stop myself.</i>

184
00:26:10,625 --> 00:26:12,291
<i>It feels so good, you know,</i>

185
00:26:12,375 --> 00:26:13,500
<i>getting rid of the scum.</i>

186
00:26:13,583 --> 00:26:14,666
What the hell?

187
00:26:17,791 --> 00:26:20,166
<i>It feels like I'm getting revenge</i>

188
00:26:20,250 --> 00:26:21,416
<i>on that little shit.</i>

189
00:26:23,958 --> 00:26:26,416
<i>Getting to choose who gets to live…</i>

190
00:26:28,125 --> 00:26:28,958
<i>and who dies.</i>

191
00:26:35,625 --> 00:26:37,916
Why the hell did he keep this?

192
00:26:47,250 --> 00:26:48,958
You know he didn't mean to.

193
00:26:51,041 --> 00:26:53,541
<i>But Uncle Sak was too damn smart, sis.</i>

194
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:56,583
<i>When he found out I'd done it again,</i>

195
00:26:56,666 --> 00:26:59,375
<i>he took the body</i>
<i>and made it look like a Phii Pong attack</i>

196
00:26:59,458 --> 00:27:00,666
<i>to trick the villagers.</i>

197
00:27:01,541 --> 00:27:04,458
<i>He set himself up as a shaman,</i>
<i>making money off them.</i>

198
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:07,708
What a piece of shit, right?

199
00:27:19,166 --> 00:27:21,416
<i>So Mom and Dad sent me off to Bangkok.</i>

200
00:27:22,291 --> 00:27:24,166
<i>They said that the city would cure me.</i>

201
00:27:50,750 --> 00:27:52,208
<i>But I was never gonna stop.</i>

202
00:27:52,291 --> 00:27:54,000
MOBILE MEDICAL VOLUNTEER UNIT
BO KLUEA, NAN

203
00:27:56,625 --> 00:27:57,541
Hello there.

204
00:27:57,625 --> 00:28:00,833
REGISTRATION

205
00:28:02,208 --> 00:28:03,708
<i>And once I became a doctor…</i>

206
00:28:03,791 --> 00:28:05,583
You can wait at the back, okay?

207
00:28:05,666 --> 00:28:08,333
<i>…it was even easier</i>
<i>to find more scum like them.</i>

208
00:28:13,625 --> 00:28:14,791
You're by yourself?

209
00:28:14,875 --> 00:28:15,875
Yes, I'm alone.

210
00:28:17,208 --> 00:28:18,625
MOBILE MEDICAL VOLUNTEER UNIT

211
00:28:18,708 --> 00:28:21,583
<i>Getting to choose who gets to live</i>

212
00:28:22,458 --> 00:28:23,791
<i>and who dies.</i>

213
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:31,583
<i>All these scum</i>

214
00:28:32,250 --> 00:28:33,750
<i>are all the fucking same.</i>

215
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:36,041
<i>Just different faces.</i>

216
00:29:02,375 --> 00:29:03,666
<i>Every single tooth</i>

217
00:29:04,416 --> 00:29:05,875
<i>that I pulled from their bodies…</i>

218
00:29:07,916 --> 00:29:10,458
<i>was a reward I gave to myself.</i>

219
00:30:20,458 --> 00:30:21,916
And did you know,

220
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:24,500
they didn't plan to send me
to Bangkok alone.

221
00:30:26,041 --> 00:30:27,416
You were supposed to go, too.

222
00:30:30,791 --> 00:30:31,708
But Uncle Sak…

223
00:30:33,416 --> 00:30:36,875
blackmailed us all about what I was doing.

224
00:30:36,958 --> 00:30:40,666
<i>Dad had to give him the money,</i>
<i>the land, everything.</i>

225
00:30:42,041 --> 00:30:43,208
<i>But it was never enough.</i>

226
00:30:43,291 --> 00:30:45,416
<i>Then he killed that kid named Mued…</i>

227
00:30:46,875 --> 00:30:50,500
<i>…and used his teeth</i>
<i>to blackmail our family for more money.</i>

228
00:30:55,041 --> 00:30:56,541
But you have revenge.

229
00:30:58,375 --> 00:30:59,458
So thank me.

230
00:31:00,166 --> 00:31:01,833
These secrets are all yours.

231
00:31:03,250 --> 00:31:05,833
But what do you want from me right now?

232
00:31:09,416 --> 00:31:10,250
Well…

233
00:31:12,458 --> 00:31:14,250
<i>Mom would never say anything.</i>

234
00:31:15,791 --> 00:31:16,625
<i>And Dad,</i>

235
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:20,041
<i>he's got one more chance</i>
<i>to protect his family.</i>

236
00:31:23,916 --> 00:31:24,916
So that leaves you.

237
00:31:32,250 --> 00:31:33,500
I won't tell anyone.

238
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:40,291
Promise, I won't.
I won't say anything. Honestly.

239
00:31:40,375 --> 00:31:41,250
I swear.

240
00:31:42,166 --> 00:31:43,500
I'm not lying, Wat.

241
00:31:44,041 --> 00:31:46,166
They all say that
when they're about to die.

242
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:48,041
Why should I believe you?

243
00:31:56,041 --> 00:31:57,208
Hey!

244
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:02,916
Narong, where's your grandson?

245
00:32:04,416 --> 00:32:05,916
- Hey, hey, uncle.
- Uncle!

246
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:07,750
- Uncle!
- Uncle! No, no, no.

247
00:32:07,833 --> 00:32:09,166
- Uncle! Uncle!
- Come back here.

248
00:32:09,958 --> 00:32:12,125
What the fuck are you doing, huh?

249
00:32:13,375 --> 00:32:14,375
Take him.

250
00:32:17,583 --> 00:32:18,416
Inspector.

251
00:32:19,583 --> 00:32:20,500
You find them?

252
00:32:20,583 --> 00:32:21,791
No sign of the kid, sir.

253
00:32:29,208 --> 00:32:30,750
Do you wanna die?

254
00:32:30,833 --> 00:32:32,708
If you're gonna shoot me, just shoot!

255
00:32:35,375 --> 00:32:36,875
Have you called for the boat yet?

256
00:32:36,958 --> 00:32:38,416
It's on the way, Inspector.

257
00:32:39,083 --> 00:32:40,375
Pull the trigger.

258
00:32:40,458 --> 00:32:42,666
Come on. Do it!

259
00:32:44,416 --> 00:32:46,666
I'm not afraid to die. Just do it!

260
00:32:46,750 --> 00:32:47,625
Shoot!

261
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:14,666
Rescue! What's your ETA?

262
00:33:20,166 --> 00:33:21,500
- Hurry up!
- Hurry up!

263
00:33:23,791 --> 00:33:24,958
Come on. Come on!

264
00:33:27,791 --> 00:33:30,458
CHIANG KHAN RESCUE UNIT

265
00:34:00,916 --> 00:34:01,750
Aim.

266
00:34:02,375 --> 00:34:03,208
Aim.

267
00:34:04,875 --> 00:34:07,208
Ms. Wan, please try to stay calm.

268
00:34:07,291 --> 00:34:09,125
- Please just stay calm.
- My son. Where is he?

269
00:34:09,208 --> 00:34:10,666
Just relax.

270
00:34:10,750 --> 00:34:12,041
Your son is okay.

271
00:34:12,916 --> 00:34:15,875
The nurse will bring him in shortly.
Don't worry.

272
00:34:16,791 --> 00:34:23,791
MRS. WANRUDEE KUDPRATHUM

273
00:34:29,625 --> 00:34:31,958
Do you remember how you got on that boat
at all?

274
00:34:39,250 --> 00:34:40,291
Mm.

275
00:34:40,916 --> 00:34:42,125
I blacked out.

276
00:34:43,416 --> 00:34:45,000
I don't remember at all.

277
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:50,708
You and your son had Midazolam
in your blood.

278
00:34:52,250 --> 00:34:53,666
It's an anesthetic.

279
00:34:53,750 --> 00:34:56,583
It causes temporary memory loss
after injection.

280
00:34:56,666 --> 00:34:59,625
You maybe dizzy and disoriented,
it's normal.

281
00:35:01,458 --> 00:35:04,583
But do you really not remember?
Who were you talking to

282
00:35:05,291 --> 00:35:07,291
right before you passed out?

283
00:35:31,583 --> 00:35:33,375
Mom tried to protect her son.

284
00:35:35,291 --> 00:35:36,291
Like you would.

285
00:35:37,291 --> 00:35:38,791
You'd do anything for Aim.

286
00:35:42,791 --> 00:35:44,875
If you had cared that day and helped me,

287
00:35:45,833 --> 00:35:47,708
maybe I wouldn't be like this.

288
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:49,833
Who knows?

289
00:35:51,208 --> 00:35:53,375
Sis, help me!

290
00:35:53,458 --> 00:35:54,958
Help me, sis.

291
00:35:55,041 --> 00:35:56,208
Help me, Wan!

292
00:35:56,291 --> 00:35:57,250
Wan!

293
00:35:57,333 --> 00:35:58,625
I told you to eat it!

294
00:35:58,708 --> 00:36:00,083
Wan.

295
00:36:00,166 --> 00:36:01,416
Help me, Wan!

296
00:36:02,666 --> 00:36:03,666
Wan!

297
00:36:05,125 --> 00:36:06,750
Go on. Eat it.

298
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:12,125
Whatever. It was a long time ago.

299
00:36:15,250 --> 00:36:16,375
But right now,

300
00:36:18,250 --> 00:36:20,708
for once, try acting like my sister.

301
00:36:32,458 --> 00:36:33,458
Be still!

302
00:37:01,833 --> 00:37:03,208
I didn't see anything.

303
00:37:08,541 --> 00:37:09,666
Okay.

304
00:37:14,833 --> 00:37:16,208
INVESTIGATION DIVISION

305
00:37:18,041 --> 00:37:19,625
You killed your son-in-law, didn't you?

306
00:37:32,583 --> 00:37:33,916
Tell me why you did it.

307
00:37:41,541 --> 00:37:42,916
But he hurt my daughter.

308
00:37:43,583 --> 00:37:44,958
I had to save her.

309
00:37:51,208 --> 00:37:52,833
What about the Phii Pong murders?

310
00:37:54,333 --> 00:37:56,000
Are you also behind them?

311
00:38:08,166 --> 00:38:10,083
Sir! Sir! Excuse me, sir.

312
00:38:10,166 --> 00:38:12,125
Please, sir, tell us the situation.

313
00:38:12,208 --> 00:38:16,166
Uh, for now, we're bringing in
all units that are nearby here

314
00:38:17,041 --> 00:38:19,791
to pursue every possible lead
on this killer.

315
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:22,125
But we admit that

316
00:38:22,208 --> 00:38:25,541
serial killer cases in this country
are not common.

317
00:38:26,208 --> 00:38:28,833
And I would like to, um, reassure everyone

318
00:38:28,916 --> 00:38:31,208
that we're doing
everything we can right now.

319
00:38:31,291 --> 00:38:33,958
Have you got any suspects yet?

320
00:38:34,041 --> 00:38:35,666
- Do you have any suspects?
- Yeah.

321
00:38:35,750 --> 00:38:37,375
- Tell us.
- Any suspects?

322
00:38:37,458 --> 00:38:39,875
Sergeant, what's going on? How's the kid?

323
00:38:39,958 --> 00:38:42,166
He's still unconscious.
Give us a hand here.

324
00:38:42,250 --> 00:38:44,375
Come on, give us a hand here, Lieutenant.

325
00:38:45,208 --> 00:38:48,625
Gentle. Easy, easy. All right.

326
00:38:48,708 --> 00:38:51,291
CHIANG KHAN RESCUE UNIT

327
00:38:53,375 --> 00:38:54,458
Inspector.

328
00:38:54,541 --> 00:38:55,750
Here's the records.

329
00:38:56,666 --> 00:39:00,000
Every province Dr. Wat lived in
matches the crime scenes.

330
00:39:01,916 --> 00:39:06,041
If it wasn't the cops,
it was the shaman around here.

331
00:39:06,125 --> 00:39:08,125
Just repeating the same thing for years

332
00:39:08,208 --> 00:39:11,875
while nobody bothered to look
for the person who killed my son.

333
00:39:11,958 --> 00:39:13,916
Back then, how do you remember him?

334
00:39:14,791 --> 00:39:16,041
I don't.

335
00:39:16,125 --> 00:39:18,291
You're all in it together, aren't you?

336
00:39:18,375 --> 00:39:20,958
You're trying to take my land off me.

337
00:39:21,041 --> 00:39:23,250
If a spirit wants you dead,

338
00:39:24,250 --> 00:39:25,875
<i>then you're dead anyway.</i>

339
00:39:25,958 --> 00:39:28,000
<i>Doesn't matter how you die, Inspector.</i>

340
00:39:31,916 --> 00:39:33,458
Or maybe you're lying.

341
00:39:34,208 --> 00:39:36,000
Which means I can't help him.

342
00:39:36,083 --> 00:39:38,625
If you think it was my husband,
then arrest him.

343
00:39:38,708 --> 00:39:40,041
Mom.

344
00:39:55,791 --> 00:39:57,625
So do you have a suspect yet?

345
00:39:58,750 --> 00:40:00,458
Yes, do you have any suspect?

346
00:40:00,541 --> 00:40:01,708
Any suspects?

347
00:40:01,791 --> 00:40:03,916
- The suspect, sir?
- Do you have a suspect or not?

348
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:05,041
- We have.
- Yeah? Who?

349
00:40:05,125 --> 00:40:06,125
- Tell us more.
- Who is it?

350
00:40:06,208 --> 00:40:08,958
We have to wait for our forensics team
to finish their work,

351
00:40:09,041 --> 00:40:11,291
a lot of these cases are very old.

352
00:40:11,375 --> 00:40:13,833
Can you at least tell us
if it was someone who lives local?

353
00:40:15,083 --> 00:40:16,708
- Right.
- Yes, tell us.

354
00:40:16,791 --> 00:40:18,208
Someone from around here?

355
00:40:18,291 --> 00:40:20,750
- Is it a local?
- I can't answer that.

356
00:40:22,875 --> 00:40:24,041
So let me reiterate.

357
00:40:25,083 --> 00:40:28,375
Our officers are working
as hard as they all can, okay?

358
00:40:28,458 --> 00:40:30,125
You can be certain of that, okay?

359
00:40:30,208 --> 00:40:31,166
Thank you so much.

360
00:40:39,333 --> 00:40:41,541
Sir, can you just answer
one more question?

361
00:40:47,416 --> 00:40:49,333
THREE MONTHS LATER

362
00:41:12,083 --> 00:41:13,083
What is it, huh?

363
00:41:17,541 --> 00:41:20,208
The village chief asked me
to give you that.

364
00:41:20,291 --> 00:41:22,041
For his son's ordination.

365
00:41:23,291 --> 00:41:24,208
Come with me?

366
00:41:26,375 --> 00:41:29,875
Think of it a farewell party
before you transfer back to Bangkok.

367
00:41:33,208 --> 00:41:34,041
Mm.

368
00:42:16,291 --> 00:42:17,333
How you doing?

369
00:42:22,375 --> 00:42:23,208
Okay.

370
00:42:27,916 --> 00:42:30,125
Now you're no longer a teacher,

371
00:42:30,208 --> 00:42:31,250
what will you do?

372
00:42:33,208 --> 00:42:36,416
Are you still investigating me, hmm?

373
00:42:42,166 --> 00:42:43,916
I haven't really thought about it.

374
00:42:45,375 --> 00:42:49,666
Taking him to school and other stuff
will fill all my time.

375
00:42:51,375 --> 00:42:53,833
Terrible traffic in Bangkok.

376
00:42:54,625 --> 00:42:55,666
Mmm.

377
00:42:57,208 --> 00:42:58,041
And you?

378
00:43:01,041 --> 00:43:03,583
Well, my place is far from the station.

379
00:43:05,291 --> 00:43:07,291
The traffic will get to me, too.

380
00:43:21,291 --> 00:43:22,208
Inspector…

381
00:43:29,125 --> 00:43:31,125
I really appreciate you saving me.

382
00:43:33,666 --> 00:43:34,666
If not for you,

383
00:43:35,583 --> 00:43:37,000
anything could have happened.

384
00:43:41,041 --> 00:43:42,291
I was just doing my job.

385
00:43:43,708 --> 00:43:44,750
I wasn't saving you.

386
00:43:50,625 --> 00:43:51,458
Hmm.

387
00:43:55,791 --> 00:43:57,666
But you can't protect him forever.

388
00:44:00,166 --> 00:44:01,375
Someone will find out.

389
00:44:09,166 --> 00:44:10,125
Find out?

390
00:44:12,666 --> 00:44:14,083
You know what I'm talking about.

391
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:40,333
- Please sit. Right.
- Hello.

392
00:44:47,625 --> 00:44:48,875
Mm. Mm.

393
00:44:58,208 --> 00:45:03,666
It's the price we agreed on
after deducting your debt, correct?

394
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:40,833
Pa.

395
00:45:45,333 --> 00:45:47,750
Aim and I are moving to Bangkok.

396
00:45:51,916 --> 00:45:53,458
This means I won't visit you,

397
00:45:54,541 --> 00:45:55,625
not often.

398
00:45:59,166 --> 00:46:02,708
Dad, so you must be well behaved.

399
00:46:06,458 --> 00:46:07,291
Mmm.

400
00:46:14,083 --> 00:46:17,458
I'm not mad at Mom and you
for what you did.

401
00:46:28,958 --> 00:46:31,958
You believe that you're better than us,
Wan, but you're not.

402
00:46:48,041 --> 00:46:49,041
Help me.

403
00:47:37,791 --> 00:47:38,791
I'm leaving.

404
00:47:41,708 --> 00:47:42,750
I'll come back to visit.

405
00:47:48,333 --> 00:47:50,333
Please take care of your family.

406
00:47:52,125 --> 00:47:55,000
Don't let anyone hurt us.

407
00:48:32,250 --> 00:48:33,458
I sold the land.

408
00:48:36,041 --> 00:48:37,375
It's all I could get, Mom.

409
00:48:58,833 --> 00:49:00,958
You heard from your brother?

410
00:49:12,875 --> 00:49:14,250
I'm leaving.

411
00:49:17,708 --> 00:49:21,000
Don't you tell anyone
about what he did, okay?

412
00:49:22,625 --> 00:49:24,458
He didn't mean to do it.

413
00:49:26,500 --> 00:49:27,791
I think he's sick.

414
00:49:29,041 --> 00:49:31,583
If you get in touch him, tell him…

415
00:49:32,625 --> 00:49:34,416
to come and see me.

416
00:50:01,416 --> 00:50:02,416
Ma.

417
00:50:05,625 --> 00:50:07,166
Could you love me more?

418
00:50:10,916 --> 00:50:11,750
Hmm?

419
00:50:15,875 --> 00:50:17,166
As much as…

420
00:50:20,333 --> 00:50:22,000
you love my brother, Mom?

421
00:50:34,166 --> 00:50:35,541
I'm so sorry…

422
00:50:37,416 --> 00:50:40,791
for letting you believe
that I love your brother more.

423
00:50:43,166 --> 00:50:45,416
He, more than you, needed me.

424
00:50:48,916 --> 00:50:49,916
I knew

425
00:50:50,625 --> 00:50:52,916
that you could get by on your own.

426
00:52:45,625 --> 00:52:46,500
Mom.

427
00:52:47,583 --> 00:52:51,291
So we're moving far away.

428
00:52:51,375 --> 00:52:55,583
Aren't you going to miss Grandpa,
Uncle Wat, and Grandma?

429
00:52:59,833 --> 00:53:00,958
I probably will.

430
00:53:04,416 --> 00:53:05,500
But I'll be fine.

431
00:53:06,916 --> 00:53:07,916
I've got you.

432
00:53:13,541 --> 00:53:17,625
NA SAO VILLAGE
NA SAO, CHIANG KHAN, LOEI
